From c50a565f5c48a243e1a75b25777dc9aea279c852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: HDR over the tunnel connected: the decision,
 the picture drawn as it is, and what fails

HDR10, HLG and HDR10+ videos go over the tunnel as YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits (videoscreen.hadeshdr10tunnel,
on) where HDR10Tunnel.h says so: the display declares 4:2:2 and HDR, the connector is HDMI of a
kernel backend with DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB, the mode is 3840x2160 at 50 or 60 Hz, the picture is
one the bridge draws as it is, nothing of the user's (a colour format, RGB at 8 bits for HDR, the HDR10
picture adapted to the display) is overridden, and what the ordinary output would send (asked once for
each mode with a TEST_ONLY commit of an HDR10 video, DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT) is RGB at 8 bits or YCbCr 4:2:0.
Anything not known is a no, and the log says which: "HDR over the tunnel: not used for this video
(code)".

The points of the native Dolby Vision path that it goes through, each read before it was touched:
- DVBRIDGE::WantsNativeOutput(picture) answers for such a picture too (a picture of Dolby Vision is
  asked first and never comes here), so that the renderer is configured native, the output is 8 bits
  (VideoOutputBitDepth()) and BeginDVBridge() runs;
- BeginDVBridge(hdr10Tunnel, guiTransfer): no Low-Latency, no HDMI 1.4b, the tunnel on in the bridge
  (CDVBridgeGLES::SetTunnel()), the capture of the previous commit, and the GUI composited for the
  transfer of the picture (PQ or HLG) instead of PQ always; an output captured for the other kind is
  put back first; the disabled state is its own;
- the renderer (LinuxRendererGLES::Configure(), RenderUpdate(), DVBridgeConfigChanged()) takes the
  HDR signalling of the picture with SetHDR() after the output is captured (HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA and,
  per frame as for any HDR video, the HDR10+ InfoFrame), and an output that takes none for it is no
  output for it; the pictures go to RenderHdr10Tunnel() (VAAPI: the planes and the colour as
  RenderPlainMapping() takes them, the place as for a picture mapped to SDR) instead of RenderDVBridge();
- CDVBridgeGLES::PrepareTunnel() draws it as it is into the picture of the transport that the GUI is
  composited over, and Pack() packs it with no metadata (the bridge, in the commit before);
- a picture of the tunnel is never kept on the screen in place of the next one, has no Dolby Vision
  information to show, and the menus in Dolby Vision, the Dolby Vision end of stream frame and the
  hand-over between videos treat it as they treat Low-Latency, not as the Standard mode;
- what fails: a tunnel that fails is turned off for the display (DisableHdr10Tunnel(): the log says
  what the driver refused it for, and it is tried again when the display changes), and not Dolby Vision,
  whose retries are not touched: DisableNativeDVOutput() turns off the tunnel while the captured output
  is its own, and the renderer calls DisableHdr10Tunnel() where it would have disabled Dolby Vision; the
  video goes on over the ordinary output.

Not in this: Dolby Vision rebuilt as HDR10 (RenderDVConversion(): not a picture that the rule takes,
"picture" in the log), the start signal with the change of mode (the tunnel is set up after the first
pictures, with its own change of mode), and the pictures of software decoding. Host tests: the
bridge (previous commits), the rule (HDR10Tunnel.h), and the refusals of the bridge; the glue is
compiled, not run: not tried on hardware.
